    "equation": "20*d(best normalized progress) + 60*d(best near-target attachment-relative joint strike quality) + 100*first task success - 25*non-tip-first - 40*terminal(log1p((displacement/0.35)^2)) - 2*integral_until_terminal(log1p((displacement/0.35)^2)) - 1*pre-success time - 100*numerical failure",
    "design": "Compact dynamic-strike cost objective. Progress bootstraps target discovery; one bounded joint-strike potential rewards proximity, attachment-relative cable speed, and strike alignment together. Every valid hit receives the same base success reward. UAV motion is handled only by two explicit negative terms: displacement from the initial UAV position at episode termination, and the time integral of that displacement before termination. A modest one-per-second deduction prefers timely strikes. Compact-hit bonuses, maximum-displacement gates, separate speed/direction rewards, effort costs, and smoothness costs are disabled.",
    "direction_shaping": "Direction enters only through the bounded joint-strike potential, together with near-target attachment-relative cable speed. Reported hard success retains the unchanged world-frame 30-degree direction gate.",
